Subject: [PATCH] Defer projection painting until a target image exists

Image cache updates can arrive before viewport initialization allocates the
prescaled QImage. Keep backend cache updates, but skip drawing into a null
image; the normal viewport allocation and prescale redraw it later.

Related upstream report (historical startup QPainter diagnostics):
https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=289419
That report was resolved; this guard addresses the current null-image path,
not a backport of its resolution.

diff --git a/libs/ui/canvas/kis_prescaled_projection.cpp b/libs/ui/canvas/kis_prescaled_projection.cpp
--- a/libs/ui/canvas/kis_prescaled_projection.cpp
+++ b/libs/ui/canvas/kis_prescaled_projection.cpp
@@ -285,7 +285,7 @@
 
 void KisPrescaledProjection::preScale()
 {
-    if (!m_d->image) return;
+    if (!m_d->image || m_d->prescaledQImage.isNull()) return;
 
     m_d->prescaledQImage.fill(0);
 
@@ -418,6 +418,8 @@
 
 void KisPrescaledProjection::updateScaledImage(KisPPUpdateInfoSP info)
 {
+    if (m_d->prescaledQImage.isNull()) return;
+
     QPainter gc(&m_d->prescaledQImage);
     gc.setCompositionMode(QPainter::CompositionMode_Source);
     drawUsingBackend(gc, info);
